Please note that this code is intended for educational purposes and should be used responsibly, ensuring that user privacy and security are respected.

### Manifest File (manifest.json)

Before using the script, you need to set up a manifest file to declare the necessary permissions for your extension.

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Password Recovery Helper",
  "version": "1.0",
  "permissions": [
    "cookies",
    "passwords",
    "activeTab"
  ],
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "background.js"
  },
  "action": {
    "default_popup": "popup.html"
  }
}
```

### Background Script (background.js)

This script will handle the collection of cookies and passwords.

```javascript
// background.js

// Function to collect cookies and passwords for the current active tab
async function collectCredentials() {
    // Get the active tab to determine the current domain
    const [tab] = await chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true });
    const domain = new URL(tab.url).hostname;

    // Collect cookies for the current domain
    chrome.cookies.getAll({ domain: domain }, (cookies) => {
        // Collect saved passwords for the current domain
        chrome.passwords.getAll({ origin: tab.url }, (passwords) => {
            // Format the data for display
            let cookieData = cookies.map(cookie => `${cookie.name}: ${cookie.value}`).join('\n');
            let passwordData = passwords.map(password => `Username: ${password.username}, Password: ${password.password}`).join('\n');

            // Display the collected data in an alert box
            alert(`Cookies for ${domain}:\n${cookieData}\n\nSaved Passwords:\n${passwordData}`);
        });
    });
}

// Listen for the extension action (button click)
chrome.action.onClicked.addListener(collectCredentials);
```

### Popup HTML (popup.html)

You can create a simple popup to trigger the collection of credentials.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Password Recovery Helper</title>
    <script src="background.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Password Recovery Helper</h1>
    <button id="collect">Collect Credentials</button>
    <script>
        document.getElementById('collect').addEventListener('click', () => {
            chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ action: "collectCredentials" });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

